    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that stuff feels so incremental and slow... like puting a bandaid on a gunshot wound. the scale of the collapse is just so much bigger than any \"community action.\" i look at the math and the tipping points and it just feels like we are just rearranging deck chairs on the titanic. i struggle to find any reason to keep investing in a world that is basically a lost cause. it's just exhausting to keep existing in a timeline that feels doomed.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
