      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your reaction to the sheer scale of the crisis and the feeling that efforts are too small is a very common and understandable response to climate despair. While individual contributions cannot instantly reverse planetary collapse, history shows that even seemingly insignificant collective actions eventually push systems past critical thresholds. Instead of viewing this as a racing countdown, consider changing your lens to focus on the long-term resilience the world builds despite the odds. Sometimes the most productive thing you can do is pause, seek support from others feeling the same, and find peace in simply being present while waiting for a future that is still being built.",
