      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your honesty about wanting to quit the struggle because \"fighting for a future that won't exist\" is actually a profound form of processing the grief of loss. Instead of judging yourself for just staying to witness the decline, try giving yourself permission to mourn the imagined end of the world before trying again in a different, perhaps more realistic, way. Recognizing that the timeline you fear might not be the only possible outcome can help shift your perspective from a hopeless spectator to someone who still holds some influence over the details. It doesn't mean pretending the apocalypse is another day; it means acknowledging that hope isn't a denial of reality, but a necessary practice for finding a way to live while it still does.",
